WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.910
RYAN MATSUMOTO: Today, we're
talking about careers, MLOps,

00:00:03.910 --> 00:00:06.080
data transfer, and communities.

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:08.440
I'm Ryan, and welcome
to This Week in Cloud,

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:11.590
where we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:13.510
The cloud computing
industry is booming,

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:15.340
and experts are in high demand.

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:18.430
To help meet this demand
and democratize opportunity,

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:21.340
Google Cloud is introducing
its first virtual certification

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:24.100
journey learning program for
underrepresented communities

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:27.670
across the United States,
Cloud Career Jump Start.

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:29.830
The program is free
of charge and includes

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:32.770
technical and professional
skill development and resources

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:35.020
to provide readiness
for certification

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:38.080
via the Google Cloud
Associate Cloud Engineer exam.

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:41.810
Check out the blog for
eligibility and details.

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:44.300
We recently published
our MLOps framework

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:46.460
to help organizations
come up to speed faster

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:47.990
in this important domain.

00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:50.600
And to help ML practitioners
translate the framework

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:53.287
into actionable steps,
we released a blog post

00:00:53.287 --> 00:00:55.370
that highlights some of
the factors that influence

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:57.170
where to begin, based
on our experience

00:00:57.170 --> 00:01:00.460
in working with customers.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:03.190
Overseeing a Cloud
migration is a tough job,

00:01:03.190 --> 00:01:05.920
but moving your actual data
there doesn't have to be.

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:08.590
With the availability of our
latest transfer appliance

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:11.020
for the US, EU, and
Singapore regions,

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:13.660
we're providing a simple,
secure, cost-effective,

00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:16.300
and offline way to
transfer petabytes of data

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:19.690
from data centers and field
locations into Google Cloud.

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:23.240
Check out the blog for use
cases and more information.

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:24.980
Helping developers
be their best is

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:26.703
core to Google Cloud's mission.

00:01:26.703 --> 00:01:28.370
So, we're excited to
announce investment

00:01:28.370 --> 00:01:31.190
in two new communities--
the Google Cloud community

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:34.370
and a partnership with
collectives on Stack Overflow.

00:01:34.370 --> 00:01:37.370
Both communities will serve
to enhance creativity, foster

00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:39.260
greater collaboration,
and contribute

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:41.480
to the overall success of
our developer community

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:43.490
and our valued customer base.

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:46.160
They'll also provide a globally
connected source of information

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:50.127
for faster answers and
recognition of contributions.

00:01:50.127 --> 00:01:52.210
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:54.650
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:55.990
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:57.800
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:00.270
We'll see you in the Cloud.

